findings.body:
The guard in `scheduleMemberWelcomeEmailJob` was flipped from `!hasScheduled.processOutbox` to `hasScheduled.processOutbox`. `hasScheduled.processOutbox` starts as `false`, so the condition is always false and `jobsService.addJob` is never reached. The flag is only set to `true` inside that same block, so it can never become true either. The worker is never registered, in any environment, and no welcome emails are ever sent from the outbox.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/member-welcome-emails/jobs/index.js" lines="8-23"}

::callout{type="warning"}
The `NODE_ENV` test guard is also wrong in the same expression. In the original it blocked scheduling under test, and as written it does nothing useful. Fix both in the same edit.

::suggestion{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/member-welcome-emails/jobs/index.js" lines="15-15"}
        if (!hasScheduled.processOutbox && !process.env.NODE_ENV.startsWith('test')) {

The original gate was `labs.isSet('welcomeEmails') && WELCOME_EMAIL_SOURCES.includes(source)`. The new gate is `welcomeEmailConfig || WELCOME_EMAIL_SOURCES.includes(source)`, which is much wider than before.

`_resolveContextSource` returns `'member'` whenever no context flags are set, so any default-context create takes the outbox branch even when `memberWelcomeEmailTestInbox` is empty (the shipped default in `defaults.json`). That writes an outbox row on every self-hosted install, which is the exact impact the PR says it avoids. Conversely, once the config is set, import, admin and API creates also write outbox rows, which should never happen.

::diff{file="ghost/core/core/server/services/members/members-api/repositories/MemberRepository.js" lines="336-345"}

The tests break under this logic. Tracing the code:
- Integration `does NOT create outbox entry when config is not set` (lines 52-65): context is `{}`, so the source is `member`, and a row is written. The assertion expects zero.
- Integration `does NOT create outbox entry when member is imported` (lines 67-80) and `... created by admin` (lines 82-95): the config is set, so `||` takes the branch and writes a row. Both expect zero.
- Unit `does NOT create outbox entry when config is not set` (lines 554-569) and `does not create outbox entry for disallowed sources` (lines 571-594): same effect.

Since `config.testing.json` sets the inbox, every test that creates a member through the default context now writes outbox rows as well.

